{
  "version": 1,
  "id": "wan22_i2v_flipbook",
  "name": "Wan 2.2 I2V — flipbook source",
  "description": "Image-to-video for the Flipbook video session: a still (a symbol region, a piece of art) drives Wan 2.2 I2V A14B, an optional BiRefNet pass cuts the background to alpha, and the result saves as an animated WEBP whose frames become a flipbook clip. Serverless-safe: every node is ComfyUI core or 1038lab/ComfyUI-RMBG, both baked into the worker image — the original graph's ImageResizeKJv2 (KJNodes, absent from the worker) is replaced by core ImageScale, pixel-identical at these settings because the KJ node was set to keep_proportion:stretch with divisible_by:2 at 320. The save node's fps is wired to the generation fps (node 192) so the preview can never drift from the motion rate. `width`/`height` are DELIBERATELY unbound: the runner fills those roles from the atlas-tool's gen_width/gen_height, which default to 1024 — injecting that into WanImageToVideo would blow up VRAM and time on an 81-frame batch. Generation size is a param instead, defaulting to the tested 640. Frame count is floor(duration * fps + 1) = 81 at the defaults.",
  "author": "iw-builtin",
  "base": "wan22-i2v",
  "kind": "video",
  "bindings": {
